fix(image): shorten exFAT label to LATHEASSETS (exFAT 11-char limit)

mkfs.exfat aborted the image build with "input string is too long /
exFAT format fail!". The shared partition label "LATHE_ASSETS" is 12
characters; exFAT volume labels are capped at 11.

Rename the label to "LATHEASSETS" (11 chars) everywhere it must agree, since
the OS mounts /assets by-label and the host launchers/installers detect the
drive by-label:

- scripts/build-usb-image.sh, modules/storage.nix, modules/iso.nix (mkfs +
  by-label mount)
- launcher/{linux,macos}, installer/{linux,macos,windows} (drive detection)
- README / RELEASE_README / SETUP / docs for consistency

Verified: no LATHE_ASSETS occurrences remain; new label is 11 chars; the
shell scripts pass bash -n.
